--- 6. CORRECTION (added 2026-11-04, later review round) ---
The installed-tree digest quoted in section 4 (2ece6ea6...) is NOT reproducible:
its aggregation recipe was never recorded, and no common recipe (path prefix,
separator, sort order, line terminator, hashing vs. raw bytes, upper/lower case)
reproduces it -- roughly 2000 combinations were tried against the same tree.
The digest is therefore WITHDRAWN as unverifiable.

The underlying measurement still holds, and is now recorded with a recipe that
a third party can recompute:

  node tools/tree_digest.mjs <clone>/apps/studio/node_modules --package-json-only

  package.json scope : 4672eb248660994f9d0ff2b8fb7d496b72c84334a0c63c18e501aa2be3c2f304  (317 files)
  whole-tree scope   : 4542171b605773bea02a2f4058a0bd7f8d057e40013e9ad4c4b72eed8afcdee3  (17191 files)

Both values were reproduced identically on THREE independent clones, one of
which is the clone this very log's section 4 was measured on -- i.e. the tree
content is confirmed unchanged; only the quoted digest string was wrong.
See docs/evidence/ATS-102/06-independent-verification.log for the raw output.
